    "notes": "1. 'total_revenue' is mapped directly from the 'Revenue' line item.\n2. 'total_operating_cost' is composed of 'Cost of sales', 'Marketing and selling expenses', 'General and administrative expenses', and 'Other operating income and expenses'. 'Other operating income and expenses' is included as a cost component because its net amount is negative (expense) in all periods, and it contains operational items like restructuring costs and asset impairments. 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is not included as it is a non-operating item.\n3. 'net_income' is mapped from 'Net profit, Group share'.\n4. 'taxes' is mapped from 'Income taxes'.\n5. 'interest_expenses' is composed of 'Cost of net financial debt' and 'Interest on lease liabilities'. 'Other financial income and expenses' is excluded as it contains non-interest items like dividends received and fair value adjustments.\n6. All values are extracted from the primary statement. Parentheses in the source indicate negative values, but per the sign convention for costs and expenses, the extracted numbers are positive as they reduce income.\n7. The scale is 1,000,000 (EUR millions) as indicated in the statement header.\n8. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns but are not used for the core consolidated values as the primary statement contains the required totals.",
